# The build context for py-endgame-aws's image is this directory rather than
# py-endgame-aws/, because that package depends on ../py-endgame by path --
# see py-endgame-aws/Makefile. This file is what keeps the rest of the repo
# out of the context; it used to live in py-endgame-aws/.dockerignore.
#
# The other projects here have their own devcontainers, but each builds with
# its own directory as the context, so none of them reads this file.

# Nothing outside the two python packages the image is built from. jobs/ is
# ~800MB of downloaded terraform providers on its own, and none of this ever
# ends up in the image, so it's pure upload.
checker/
jobs/
matcher/
py-launcher/
internet/
.git/
.github/

# `**/` on all of these: an unanchored pattern in .dockerignore matches from
# the context root only, and everything worth dropping is a directory or two
# down now.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.venv/
**/scratch/

# NOTE: py-endgame-aws/config.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
# endgame_aws/config.py resolves it relative to the package root, so the
# deployed image needs it at /home/dev/runtime/config.json -- main.py reads it
# at import time.

# Machine-local settings, deliberately not baked into a deployed image.
**/*.env
